{
 "name": "CRM · Upsert lead",
 "nodes": [
  {
   "parameters": {
    "content": "## CRM · Upsert lead (Lesson 5.9)\nCalled by every engine when a business lead appears (outreach reply, Instagram comment, WhatsApp, email). One sub-workflow, so every channel creates leads the same way.\n1 Normalise email (lowercase), phone (+234...), domain (no www.)\n2 Company: search by domain -> found? update : create\n3 Contact: Create or Update (by email) with lead_source and consent\n4 Associate contact <-> company\n5 Buying intent and no open deal for this company -> deal at New enquiry, owner Tolu, associated to both\n6 Supabase: save crm_contact_id and crm_deal_id\nThen the score (code, calibrated on last quarter; outside the zone is a knock-out rule) is written to harvest_score. Ready and below Sales qualified lead -> SQL, a Call today task and a Telegram ping.\nThis workflow never writes dealstage, so it can't start the stage-change workflow.\n\nCredentials: HubSpot App Token credential (the \"n8n Growth Desk\" private app token, with only contact, company and deal read/write scopes, plus tasks if you create tasks) on every HubSpot node and HTTP Request; Postgres; Telegram.\nPlaceholders: YOUR_STAGE_ID_NEW_ENQUIRY, YOUR_TOLU_OWNER_ID, YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.\nHubSpot free: about 100 requests per 10 seconds per private app. Test on a test portal or a few test records first.",
    "height": 540,
    "width": 660
   },
   "id": "385eed7b-b8e1-4bab-8cb2-51971469aabb",
   "name": "Note 1",
